# A C header in a SUBDIRECTORY of an include root, reached by the spelling a C
# programmer would already write. Compiled with `-Itest/ffi_headers/`.
#
# Before feature-n-a-c-header-import-cannot-name-a-header-in-a-subdirectory the
# only form that reached such a header was the ABSOLUTE
# `import "/usr/include/SDL2/SDL.h"`, which hardcodes one distribution's layout
# into the source -- so a showcase program stopped being portable in the act of
# working. Every other spelling missed by construction, because a bare name is
# reduced to its basename before any probe runs.
import "sub/marker.h"
print(FFI_MARKER)
